  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Homoleptic complexes are compounds in which all the ligands bound to the central metal atom or ion are identical.</p><p>Homoleptic complexes have only one type of ligand.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> has only one type of ligand.</p><p>Hence, option A is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
